@title Postmortem: late daily sales dashboards
@subtitle Analytics Platform team · Juniper Retail · 2026-10-02

# Impact

- 9 hours of delay. The dashboards are normally ready by 02:00.
- 23 dashboards stale.
- The 08:00 executive sales report went out with the previous day's numbers.

# Pipeline

diagram sales dir=LR title="Daily sales pipeline"
sales: orders "Orders DB" db
sales: cdc "CDC Connector" svc
sales: kafka "Kafka" queue
sales: spark "Spark Job" job "failed: out of memory" focus
sales: warehouse "Warehouse" store
sales: dash "Dashboards" ext
sales: orders -> cdc
sales: cdc -> kafka
sales: kafka -> spark : orders topic
sales: spark -> warehouse
sales: warehouse -> dash

# Timeline

table = Time,Event; 01:00,nightly Spark Job starts; 01:47,Spark Job fails with out-of-memory on the orders partition for 2026-10-01; 02:30,automatic retry also fails; 07:55,analyst reports stale dashboards; 08:20,on-call doubles executor memory to 16 GB and reruns; 10:05,Spark Job succeeds; 10:58,dashboards refreshed

# Root cause

A promotion produced 3.4 times the normal order volume: 4.1 million orders against a typical 1.2 million. The executors had 8 GB each, which was not enough for that volume.

# Lessons learned

What went well:

- On-call recovered the pipeline with more executor memory.
- The dashboards were fully refreshed by 10:58.

What did not go well:

- The nightly job failed twice without paging anyone.
- Analysts found the stale data before the team did.
- The dashboards had no freshness banner.

# Action items

1. Page on-call when the nightly job fails twice.
2. Size executor memory from the input volume.
3. Add a data freshness banner to dashboards.
